            <ArticleTitle>A simplified and scalable synthesis of artesunate.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>63-68</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00706-016-1865-9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="ABSTRACT" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">An efficient and economically viable approach for the large-scale conversion of artemisinin into the antimalarial frontline drug artesunate was developed. This advanced synthesis includes an NaBH4-induced reduction, followed by an esterification with succinic anhydride under basic conditions. The entire conversion follows the principles of green chemistry, i.e., application of reusable solvents.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="GRAPHICAL ABSTRACT" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED"/>
            </Abstract>
